{"t":13643,"o":"\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[8B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mLakes\u001b[9Gare\u001b[13Gsome\u001b[18Gof\u001b[21Gthe\u001b[25Gmost\u001b[30Gvaried\u001b[37Gbodies\u001b[44Gof\u001b[47Gwater\u001b[53Gon\u001b[56GEarth.\u001b[63GSome\u001b[68Gsit\u001b[72Gin\u001b[75Gtectonic\u001b[84Grifts,\u001b[91Glike\u001b[96GLake\u001b[101GBaikal\u001b[108Gin\u001b[111GSiberia,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwhich\u001b[9Gholds\u001b[15Gabout\u001b[21Ga\u001b[23Gfifth\u001b[29Gof\u001b[32Gthe\u001b[36Gworld's\u001b[44Gunfrozen\u001b[53Gfresh\u001b[59Gwater\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gis\u001b[72Galso\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gdeepest\u001b[89Glake\u001b[94Gat\u001b[97Gover\u001b[102G1,600\u001b[108Gmeters.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOthers\u001b[10Gformed\u001b[17Gwhen\u001b[22Gglaciers\u001b[31Gscraped\u001b[39Gout\u001b[43Gbasins\u001b[50Gand\u001b[54Gthen\u001b[59Gmelted,\u001b[67Gleaving\u001b[75Gbehind\u001b[82Gthe\u001b[86Glong,\u001b[92Gnarrow\u001b[99Glakes\u001b[105Gof\u001b[108GScotland\u001b[117Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[7GFinger\u001b[14GLakes\u001b[20Gof\u001b[23GNew\u001b[27GYork.\u001b[33GStill\u001b[39Gothers\u001b[46Gare\u001b[50Gshaped\u001b[57Gby\u001b[60Gvolcanoes,\u001b[71Glandslides,\u001b[83Gor\u001b[86Gbeavers,\u001b[95Gand\u001b[99Gmany\u001b[104Gare\u001b[108Gtemporary,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfilling\u001b[11Gand\u001b[15Gvanishing\u001b[25Gwith\u001b[30Gthe\u001b[34Gseasons.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BLakes\u001b[9Galso\u001b[14Gwork\u001b[19Gas\u001b[22Gsmall,\u001b[29Gself-contained\u001b[44Gworlds.\u001b[52GWater\u001b[58Glayers\u001b[65Gby\u001b[68Gtemperature\u001b[80Gin\u001b[83Gsummer,\u001b[91Gwith\u001b[96Gwarm,\u001b[102Goxygen-rich\u001b[114Gwater\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bon\u001b[6Gtop\u001b[10Gand\u001b[14Gcold,\u001b[20Gdense\u001b[26Gwater\u001b[32Gsinking\u001b[40Gbelow,\u001b[47Gand\u001b[51Gthese\u001b[57Glayers\u001b[64Gmix\u001b[68Gagain\u001b[74Gin\u001b[77Gspring\u001b[84Gand\u001b[88Gautumn.\u001b[96GThat\u001b[101Gcycle\u001b[107Gdrives\u001b[114Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bnutrient\u001b[12Gflow\u001b[17Gthat\u001b[22Gfeeds\u001b[28Gfish,\u001b[34Ginsects,\u001b[43Gbirds,\u001b[50Gand\u001b[54Gthe\u001b[58Gplants\u001b[65Galong\u001b[71Gthe\u001b[75Gshore.\u001b[82GBecause\u001b[90Glakes\u001b[96Gtrap\u001b[101Gsediment,\u001b[111Gthey\u001b[116Galso\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bact\u001b[7Gas\u001b[10Gnatural\u001b[18Garchives:\u001b[28Gscientists\u001b[39Gread\u001b[44Gpollen,\u001b[52Gash,\u001b[57Gand\u001b[61Gchemical\u001b[70Gtraces\u001b[77Gin\u001b[80Gtheir\u001b[86Gmuddy\u001b[92Gbottoms\u001b[100Gto\u001b[103Greconstruct\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bclimate\u001b[11Gand\u001b[15Gvegetation\u001b[26Ggoing\u001b[32Gback\u001b[37Gthousands\u001b[47Gof\u001b[50Gyears.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BPeople\u001b[10Ghave\u001b[15Galways\u001b[22Gbeen\u001b[27Gdrawn\u001b[33Gto\u001b[36Glakes,\u001b[43Gfor\u001b[47Gdrinking\u001b[56Gwater,\u001b[63Gfishing,\u001b[72Gtrade\u001b[78Groutes,\u001b[86Gand\u001b[90Gsimply\u001b[97Gfor\u001b[101Gthe\u001b[105Gstillness\u001b[115Gthey\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Boffer.\u001b[10GThey\u001b[15Gare\u001b[19Galso\u001b[24Gfragile.\u001b[33GRunoff\u001b[40Gfrom\u001b[45Gfarms\u001b[51Gand\u001b[55Gcities\u001b[62Gadds\u001b[67Gnutrients\u001b[77Gthat\u001b[82Gcan\u001b[86Gtrigger\u001b[94Galgae\u001b[100Gblooms,\u001b[108Gwarming\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btemperatures\u001b[16Gchange\u001b[23Ghow\u001b[27Gwater\u001b[33Gmixes,\u001b[40Gand\u001b[44Gdrought\u001b[52Gcan\u001b[56Gshrink\u001b[63Ga\u001b[65Glake\u001b[70Guntil\u001b[76Gits\u001b[80Gshoreline\u001b[90Gis\u001b[93Gfar\u001b[97Gfrom\u001b[102Gwhere\u001b[108Git\u001b[111Gonce\u001b[116Gwas.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BLakes\u001b[9Gcan\u001b[13Gtake\u001b[18Ga\u001b[20Glong\u001b[25Gtime\u001b[30Gto\u001b[33Grecover\u001b[41Gonce\u001b[46Gdamaged,\u001b[55Gwhich\u001b[61Gis\u001b[64Gwhy\u001b[68Gprotecting\u001b[79Gthem\u001b[84Gtends\u001b[90Gto\u001b[93Gpay\u001b[97Goff\u001b[101Gover\u001b[106Ggenerations.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCooked for 4s · done 22:41\r\u001b[14B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B❯ \r\u001b[21C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m? for shortcuts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[45;1H\u001b[43;3H\u001b[?25h"}
{"t":16194,"mark":"replied","screen":[""," ▐▛███▛█   Claude Code v2.1.318","▝▜██████▀  Haiku 5.5 · Claude Ultra"," ▝▝   ▝▝   ~\\agent-box · /rc","","","❯ Write three short paragraphs about lakes. No tools.                                                                   ","","● Lakes are some of the most varied bodies of water on Earth. Some sit in tectonic rifts, like Lake Baikal in Siberia,","  which holds about a fifth of the world's unfrozen fresh water and is also the deepest lake at over 1,600 meters.","  Others formed when glaciers scraped out basins and then melted, leaving behind the long, narrow lakes of Scotland and","  the Finger Lakes of New York. Still others are shaped by volcanoes, landslides, or beavers, and many are temporary,","  filling and vanishing with the seasons.","","  Lakes also work as small, self-contained worlds. Water layers by temperature in summer, with warm, oxygen-rich water","  on top and cold, dense water sinking below, and these layers mix again in spring and autumn. That cycle drives the","  nutrient flow that feeds fish, insects, birds, and the plants along the shore. Because lakes trap sediment, they also","  act as natural archives: scientists read pollen, ash, and chemical traces in their muddy bottoms to reconstruct","  climate and vegetation going back thousands of years.","","  People have always been drawn to lakes, for drinking water, fishing, trade routes, and simply for the stillness they","  offer. They are also fragile. Runoff from farms and cities adds nutrients that can trigger algae blooms, warming","  temperatures change how water mixes, and drought can shrink a lake until its shoreline is far from where it once was.","  Lakes can take a long time to recover once damaged, which is why protecting them tends to pay off over generations.","","✻ Cooked for 4s · done 22:41","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","❯ ","────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","  ⏸ manual mode on · ? for shortcuts"],"cursor":[2,42]}
